x64/
.vs/
*.obj
*.user
*.log
scratch/
*.zip

# The paper is not published from this repository. Keep manuscript sources out of
# it: drafts live in the private research tree, and this repo carries the tool.
# The built PDF is the same class of file as its source, and a binary that would
# churn a diff on every rebuild: 2026-09-05, a `git add .` swept three manuscript
# PDFs and a letter draft in here, because only the sources were listed.
*.tex
*.bbl
*.aux
*.pdf
# ...and the drafts that are markdown rather than TeX -- a letter to a referee,
# a manuscript kept in .md. Scoped to those names on purpose: a blanket *.md
# would fight the "the ReadMe is tracked too" rule below and would silently
# swallow every future docs/ spec and case ReadMe.
docs/P1F_*.md
docs/email_*.md

# runs\: a case folder carries its run.bat and nothing else. Every file a run
# produces -- the RESULT records and the .log -- is written straight to
# AllResults\, and anything transient a long sweep leaves behind stays untracked.
runs/**
!runs/**/
!runs/**/*.bat
# The ReadMe is tracked too: the log no longer explains itself, so every description
# that used to be printed lives in the case ReadMe now.
!runs/**/ReadMe.md

# regression\: the bats, the two comparators and the frozen
# result_expected.txt files are tracked; a case's fresh output and its dumps
# are not.
regression/**/result.txt
regression/**/result_pfile.txt
# a multi-run case names one RESULT per block (result133.txt, result1777.txt, ...); the digit
# keeps this clear of the frozen result_expected.txt
regression/**/result[0-9]*.txt
regression/**/tmp.txt
regression/**/*.diff

# AllResults\: TRACKED in full -- the finished census output, the catalog that merges
# it, and AllResults\ReadMe.md describing both. Large (~13 MB), but a baseline that a
# fresh run is compared against is worth carrying: regenerating it costs days of
# compute. Nothing in there is edited by hand; a file changes only when the runs\
# case that produces it is re-run. .gitattributes pins those .txt files to -text so
# their bytes survive the round trip unchanged. See AllResults\ReadMe.md.
